1
00:00:05,261 --> 00:00:09,531
Upload your inspection reports
Export the IV curve CSV from each SUN2000 inverter, then drag and drop the files here, or press Upload.

2
00:00:09,731 --> 00:00:14,752
Drag and drop the CSV files
Select one or more inverter reports and drop them anywhere on the page. Files are read locally.

3
00:00:14,952 --> 00:00:19,770
Read the summary at a glance
Active strings, open circuits, abnormal Voc, low fill factor and insulation status across all inverters.

4
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:25,065
Work through the prioritised checklist
Issues are ranked by severity, with the evidence and the recommended field action. Click a string to open its curve.

5
00:00:25,265 --> 00:00:35,923
Spot weak strings on the string map
Every cell is a string. Switch views to compare status, fill factor, Voc against the inverter median, or lifetime energy.

6
00:00:36,123 --> 00:00:45,603
Inspect the I–V and P–V curves
The selected string (blue) is compared with the other active strings (grey). Pmax is marked, hover for exact points.

7
00:00:45,803 --> 00:00:49,213
Built-in data logic checks
Ten rule-based checks (R1 to R10) warn you when a scan looks unreliable, so you do not chase a false alarm.

8
00:00:49,413 --> 00:00:52,727
Check inverter health
Insulation resistance against its minimum limit, fault and grid-fault hours, and the estimated unharvested energy.

9
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:56,810
Copy the checklist into your report
One click copies every finding and recommended action as plain text, ready for your inspection report or email.
